# Diagnostics
```
invalid-define-component.ts:6:11 lint/nursery/useVueTypedObjectProps ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! This prop is declared with Object but has no TypeScript type.
  
    4 │ export default defineComponent({
    5 │   props: {
  > 6 │     user: Object,
      │           ^^^^^^
    7 │     items: { type: Array },
    8 │   },
  
  i TypeScript only knows that the prop is an object, not which properties it has, so it can't catch mistakes when the prop is passed or used.
  
  i Add the type with PropType from vue, for example Object as PropType<User>.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

